","The relationship used to estimate the mass fraction of air (O2) required for a mixture to be flammable, and, based this, estimate the overall range-range range of the air-to-gas ratio, is the **Bunker-Adam-Krud-Basset (KBT-B) method**.

Here here to show the formula:

**Equation:**

**F<sub>B</sub> = (F<sub>A</sub> + F<sub>B</sub>) / (1 - F<sub>A</sub> - F<sub>B</sub>)**

Where:

*   F<sub>B</sub> =  The molar fraction of the gas (the substance you to to to to the air) needed to achieve saturation of oxygen in air.
