**Standard Free Energy (ΔG) and Metabolic Molecules**

Standard free energy (ΔG) is a measure of the tendency of a reaction to occur in a closed system at constant temperature and pressure.  In metabolic reactions, it indicates the amount of energy released (or needed) when a bond is formed (or broken).  A more-negative ΔG means a more-bonded, more stable molecule, and the release of energy when it bonds to another molecule.

