The problem is given in terms of 2 moles of H₂ and 1 mole of O₂. The calculated ΔG<sub>rx</sub> is for 1 mole of H₂O.

Since the reaction is stoichiometric, the change in Gibbs entropy is proportional to the number of moles of the product formed.

